  :tasks [
    (:task
      :id "TaskDaemon001"
      :phase "phase-385"
      :title "Thread-Safe ProcessRegistry & Quota-Capped TwoTierSpool Core"
      :state :completed
      :completedAt 1788938500
      :priority "critical"
      :lane "engine-core"
      :concurrency "parallel-wave-1"
      :dependsOn []
            :motivation "Ensure deterministic execution and invariant conformance for Thread-Safe ProcessRegistry & Quota-Capped TwoTierSpool Core"
      :purpose "Implement ProcessRegistry class and TwoTierSpool in asl/bin/asl-engine. Background worker thread non-blockingly drains subprocess stdout/stderr, pushes to RingBuffer, and appends to quota-capped disk spool. Maintain process metadata: pid, pgid, cmd, state (running/exited/killed/timeout), start_time, cpu_percent, rss_bytes, exit_code."
      :context "Thread-Safe ProcessRegistry & Quota-Capped TwoTierSpool Core within system lifecycle"
      :outcomes [
        "Thread-safe process registration with mutex lock protecting concurrent reads and writes."
        "TwoTierSpool with in-memory RingBuffer (5,000 lines) and disk spool file (/tmp/asl_spool_<id>.log)."
      ]
      :invariants ["c1" "c2" "c3" "c4" "c5" "d34" "d46" "d51" "d52"]
      :variations [
        "Standard deterministic execution within phase boundaries"
      ]
      :failureModes [
        "Assertion failure or syntax delimiter imbalance in owned files"
      ]
      :adr "ADR-0042"
      :decision "d42"
      :actionDag [
        "Execute task work items"
        "Verify gate assertions"
      ]
:owns ["asl/bin/asl-engine"]
      :scope ["asl-engine" "process-registry" "spool-storage"]
      :targetConsumers ["all-agents" "claude-code" "antigravity" "cursor" "factory-droid" "cli"]
      :rationale "Autonomous agents lose control of background tasks launched via subshells. Uncontrolled background logs fill disk partitions or leak orphan processes when sessions end. We need a thread-safe registry with low-latency RAM ring buffers and disk quota protection."
      :acceptanceCriteria [
        "Thread-safe process registration with mutex lock protecting concurrent reads and writes."
        "TwoTierSpool with in-memory RingBuffer (5,000 lines) and disk spool file (/tmp/asl_spool_<id>.log)."
        "Disk spool quota protection: configurable ceiling (default 50MB) with automatic head truncation marker '[... earlier spool lines truncated ...] ' to prevent disk exhaustion."
        "Process group isolation (start_new_session=True) ensuring child subprocesses can be signaled as a group."
        "Automatic orphan cleanup: daemon atexit and signal handlers terminate registered active process groups."
      ]
      :gate "python3 -c \"open('asl/bin/asl-engine').read(); print('Engine Core Syntax OK')\""
      :spec "Implement ProcessRegistry class and TwoTierSpool in asl/bin/asl-engine. Background worker thread non-blockingly drains subprocess stdout/stderr, pushes to RingBuffer, and appends to quota-capped disk spool. Maintain process metadata: pid, pgid, cmd, state (running/exited/killed/timeout), start_time, cpu_percent, rss_bytes, exit_code.")

    (:task
      :id "TaskDaemon002"
      :phase "phase-385"
      :title "Complete Process Supervision RPC Interface & Fast-Wait Ergonomics"
      :state :completed
      :completedAt 1788938500
      :priority "critical"
      :lane "engine-rpc"
      :concurrency "sequential-wave-2"
      :dependsOn ["TaskDaemon001"]
            :motivation "Ensure deterministic execution and invariant conformance for Complete Process Supervision RPC Interface & Fast-Wait Ergonomics"
      :purpose "Wire RPC handlers for :proc-spawn, :proc-list, :proc-status, :proc-skeleton, :proc-read, :proc-find, :proc-input, :proc-signal, and :procWait into SovereignEngine.handle_payload() in asl/bin/asl-engine. Ensure clean ASN S-expression formatting and closed error codes (:ERR_PROC_NOT_FOUND, :ERR_SPAWN_FAILED)."
      :context "Complete Process Supervision RPC Interface & Fast-Wait Ergonomics within system lifecycle"
      :outcomes [
        "Thread-safe process registration with mutex lock protecting concurrent reads and writes."
        ":procSpawn supports :cmd, :id, :cwd, :timeout-ms, :daemon, and :waitMs (if process finishes within wait-ms, return output immediately; otherwise detach to background)."
        ":procList returns compact table of all active and finished processes with PID, runtime, RSS MB, state."
        ":procStatus :id returns live execution state, exit code, CPU%, and memory."
        ":procSkeleton :id returns high-SNR summary: total lines count, detected error/panic lines count, head 10 lines, tail 20 lines."
        ":procRead :id :start n :end m returns exact windowed slice of process output."
        ":procFind :id :query 'q' returns matching lines with line numbers using BM25/token search."
        ":procInput :id :data '...' writes bytes into process stdin stream non-blockingly."
        ":procSignal :id :signal 'SIGTERM|SIGKILL|SIGINT' dispatches signal to process group."
        ":procWait :id :timeoutMs n blocks until process exits or timeout expires."
      ]
      :invariants ["c1" "c2" "c3" "c4" "c5" "d34" "d46" "d51" "d52"]
      :variations [
        "Standard deterministic execution within phase boundaries"
      ]
      :failureModes [
        "Assertion failure or syntax delimiter imbalance in owned files"
      ]
      :adr "ADR-0042"
      :decision "d42"
      :actionDag [
        "Execute task work items"
        "Verify gate assertions"
      ]
:owns ["asl/bin/asl-engine"]
      :scope ["asl-engine" "rpc-handlers" "batch-protocol"]
      :targetConsumers ["all-agents" "claude-code" "antigravity" "cursor" "cli"]
      :rationale "Agents need structured non-bloating operations to monitor and interact with processes. Dumping raw logs causes severe context decay. Fast-wait ergonomics allow quick commands to finish synchronously within the same turn without polling."
      :acceptanceCriteria [
        "Thread-safe process registration with mutex lock protecting concurrent reads and writes."
        ":procSpawn supports :cmd, :id, :cwd, :timeout-ms, :daemon, and :waitMs (if process finishes within wait-ms, return output immediately; otherwise detach to background)."
        ":procList returns compact table of all active and finished processes with PID, runtime, RSS MB, state."
        ":procStatus :id returns live execution state, exit code, CPU%, and memory."
        ":procSkeleton :id returns high-SNR summary: total lines count, detected error/panic lines count, head 10 lines, tail 20 lines."
        ":procRead :id :start n :end m returns exact windowed slice of process output."
        ":procFind :id :query 'q' returns matching lines with line numbers using BM25/token search."
        ":procInput :id :data '...' writes bytes into process stdin stream non-blockingly."
        ":procSignal :id :signal 'SIGTERM|SIGKILL|SIGINT' dispatches signal to process group."
        ":procWait :id :timeoutMs n blocks until process exits or timeout expires."
      ]
      :gate "asl rpc '(:batch (:procList))' | grep -q ':status \"ok\"'"
      :spec "Wire RPC handlers for :proc-spawn, :proc-list, :proc-status, :proc-skeleton, :proc-read, :proc-find, :proc-input, :proc-signal, and :procWait into SovereignEngine.handle_payload() in asl/bin/asl-engine. Ensure clean ASN S-expression formatting and closed error codes (:ERR_PROC_NOT_FOUND, :ERR_SPAWN_FAILED).")

    (:task
      :id "TaskDaemon003"
      :phase "phase-385"
      :title "Multi-User Socket Discovery, Stale Socket Recovery & Auto-Bootstrap in CLI"
      :state :completed
      :completedAt 1788938500
      :priority "high"
      :lane "cli-dispatch"
      :concurrency "parallel-wave-1"
      :dependsOn []
            :motivation "Ensure deterministic execution and invariant conformance for Multi-User Socket Discovery, Stale Socket Recovery & Auto-Bootstrap in CLI"
      :purpose "Refactor get_socket_path() and ensure_daemon_running() in asl/asl. Implement get_global_socket_path() using user isolation (/tmp/asl_${USER}_global.sock). Add stale socket probe with timeout. Support --global flag in 'asl engine start|stop|status'."
      :context "Multi-User Socket Discovery, Stale Socket Recovery & Auto-Bootstrap in CLI within system lifecycle"
      :outcomes [
        "Socket hierarchy: 1. $ASL_ENGINE_SOCK override; 2. User-scoped global socket /tmp/asl_${USER}_global.sock (or ~/.asl/engine.sock); 3. Workspace-scoped socket /tmp/asl_mem_${HASH}.sock."
        "Stale socket self-healing: before connecting, perform 100ms (:ping) probe; if connection is refused, unlink dead socket and PID file automatically."
        "Auto-bootstrap: if no daemon is running, 'asl rpc' or 'asl engine start --global' transparently spawns the global system daemon in the background."
        "'asl engine status' reports socket path, PID, uptime, active process count, and memory usage."
        "'asl engine stop' cleanly flushes VFS buffers, signals child processes, and unlinks sockets."
      ]
      :invariants ["c1" "c2" "c3" "c4" "c5" "d34" "d46" "d51" "d52"]
      :variations [
        "Standard deterministic execution within phase boundaries"
      ]
      :failureModes [
        "Assertion failure or syntax delimiter imbalance in owned files"
      ]
      :adr "ADR-0042"
      :decision "d42"
      :actionDag [
        "Execute task work items"
        "Verify gate assertions"
      ]
:owns ["asl/asl"]
      :scope ["asl-cli" "socket-resolution" "daemon-lifecycle"]
      :targetConsumers ["developer-terminals" "multi-user-hosts" "agent-runners" "ci-environments"]
      :rationale "Hardcoding a shared /tmp socket causes permission errors on multi-user machines. Dead sockets left after crashes block agents from connecting. The CLI needs deterministic socket resolution, fast ping liveness checks, and transparent auto-bootstrap."
      :acceptanceCriteria [
        "Socket hierarchy: 1. $ASL_ENGINE_SOCK override; 2. User-scoped global socket /tmp/asl_${USER}_global.sock (or ~/.asl/engine.sock); 3. Workspace-scoped socket /tmp/asl_mem_${HASH}.sock."
        "Stale socket self-healing: before connecting, perform 100ms (:ping) probe; if connection is refused, unlink dead socket and PID file automatically."
        "Auto-bootstrap: if no daemon is running, 'asl rpc' or 'asl engine start --global' transparently spawns the global system daemon in the background."
        "'asl engine status' reports socket path, PID, uptime, active process count, and memory usage."
        "'asl engine stop' cleanly flushes VFS buffers, signals child processes, and unlinks sockets."
      ]
      :gate "bash -n asl/asl && asl engine status | grep -qE '(Status|Socket|Offline|Online)'"
      :spec "Refactor get_socket_path() and ensure_daemon_running() in asl/asl. Implement get_global_socket_path() using user isolation (/tmp/asl_${USER}_global.sock). Add stale socket probe with timeout. Support --global flag in 'asl engine start|stop|status'.")

